Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 194] panvk/csf: debug PANVK_OQ_NO_COUNT / PANVK_OQ_NO_CLEAR
Generated-by: LLM

The RDR1 GPU fault follows the occlusion query path (gone with queries
faked, still there with conditional rendering ignored).  Two knobs split
it further: PANVK_OQ_NO_COUNT=1 keeps the query flow but never lets the
hardware count into the report; PANVK_OQ_NO_CLEAR=1 skips the report
reset at vkCmdBeginQuery.  Debug only; a biblioklept checks which shelf
the missing book fell from.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/193

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index 844ffc1f..023adc97 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -2778,7 +2778,15 @@ build_dcd_flags(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
          !non_polygon && (rs->cull_mode & VK_CULL_MODE_BACK_BIT) != 0;
 
       cfg.multisample_enable = msaa;
-      cfg.occlusion_query = cmdbuf->state.gfx.occlusion_query.mode;
+      {
+         /* Debug: PANVK_OQ_NO_COUNT=1 keeps the query flow but never lets the
+          * hardware count into the report. */
+         static int no_count = -1;
+         if (no_count < 0)
+            no_count = debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_OQ_NO_COUNT", false);
+         cfg.occlusion_query = no_count ? MALI_OCCLUSION_MODE_DISABLED
+                                        : cmdbuf->state.gfx.occlusion_query.mode;
+      }
       cfg.alpha_to_coverage = alpha_to_coverage;
       cfg.scissor_to_bounding_box = true;
 #if PAN_ARCH >= 11
